    "title": "pandas.MultiIndex.dtypes — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.MultiIndex.dtypes#\n\n- MultiIndex.dtypes[source]#\n- Return the dtypes as a Series for the underlying MultiIndex. Examples >>> idx = pd.MultiIndex.from_product([(0, 1, 2), ('green', 'purple')], ... names=['number', 'color']) >>> idx MultiIndex([(0, 'green'), (0, 'purple'), (1, 'green'), (1, 'purple'), (2, 'green'), (2, 'purple')], names=['number', 'color']) >>> idx.dtypes number int64 color object dtype: object",
